\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hits 3-month low against euro, yen retreats. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sumeet Desai \par \uc2 848 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 2001\par 14:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 10 (Reuters) - The dollar fell to three month lows against the euro for a second straight day on Friday, extending the previous day's dizzying drop plagued by worries about the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  But it still gained more than a third of a percent against the yen after Japan's Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa described the greenback's sharp drop to two-month lows against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday as not normal. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's slide this week started after the Federal Reserve's Beige Book painted a bleak picture of the U.S. economy on Wednesday and renewed warnings by U.S. manufacturers that the strength of the dollar was hurting competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  "Euro/dollar has had a great run, it's because people are questioning whether the U.S. will rebound quickly," said Francesca Fornasari, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Lehman Brothers. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone got very excited after the Beige Book which suggested economic weakness was spreading." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the breach of key chart support levels in thin volumes had accelerated the dollar's fall, sending it on Thursday to its lowest in over three months against the Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell as far as $0.8955 per euro , its weakest performance since May 4. \par \par \uc2  It was up to around 122.25 yen at 1147 GMT, still holding within a yen of Thursday's two-month lows around 121.35 yen. The dollar suffered its biggest one day drop on Thursday against the yen since May 23. \par \par \uc2  GREENBACK AT TURNING POINT? \par \par \uc2  The dollar's latest slide has the market awash with talk that the greenback's six-year bull run has finally come to an end. \par \par \uc2  Dollar bears said the weaker outlook for the U.S. economy and a possibility that the U.S. administration could abandon its strong dollar policy because complaints from U.S. manufacturers justified a weaker greenback. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, a senior excutive from General Motors added his voice to industry calls for a change in Washington's strong dollar policy. \par \par \uc2  But others said they had heard such talk of an end to a strong dollar before and said economic fundamentals in Europe and especially Japan were worse than that in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone and their dog is talking about the end of dollar strength," said Julian Jessop, treasury economist at Standard Chartered. \par \par \uc2  "But I'm more sceptical. There's little doubt the dollar's overvalued but the data in Europe and Japan is actually worse." \par \par \uc2  Analysts noted that the dollar's decline against the euro also coincided with a drop in U.S. Treasury two-year yields to an eight-year low, though this probably also reflected the pessimism about near-term recovery in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said much of the euro's rise so far had come from speculative accounts suggesting fund managers were still not so underweight dollars - a fact which could work against the greenback in the days to come. \par \par \uc2  SHIOKAWA HINTS AT \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Analysts said that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in particular would not favour a stronger yen given the government's monthly economic report published Thursday downgraded its assessment of the economy for the sixth time this year because of weaker exports. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat, Haruhiko Kuroda said there was no need for the yen to strengthen against the dollar and the euro. \par \par \uc2  Japan's Shiokawa described the dollar's rise of around three yen on Thursday as not normal and that he sensed market manipulation. He called on the Bank of Japan to watch \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates vigilantly. \par \par \uc2  "They would definitely be ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the dollar started trending lower and trading around 119 (yen)," said Jesper Dannesboe, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials also appeared to be stepping up pressure on the BOJ to ease policy after its meeting early next week. \par \par \uc2  BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami was quoted as saying that the BOJ would try and take steps to boost inflation toward zero but added that he did not think households were concerned with falling prices. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's sharp fall against the yen on Thursday began with a break of major support at 122.80 yen which tripped stop-loss offers and drew a large sell order, rumoured at $1.0 billion, from a U.S. momentum fund. \par \par \uc2  From there stop-loss orders just cascaded as supports at 122.50 and 122.10 cracked, taking it to two-month lows at 121.35, all within the space of 30 minutes, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The euro was also seen drawing some support from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monthly bulletin a day ago which was seen in some quarters as less hawkish than expected. \par \par \uc2  While sticking with the line that interest rates were at appropriate levels, the bank did concede that the economic outlook for the second half of the year was increasingly uncertain and pledged to monitor developments closely. \par \par \uc2  Traders were waiting for the release of U.S. PPI data for July at 1230 GMT. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010810dx8a00nxh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
