\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro turns higher, reclaiming ground against yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Christina Fincher \par \uc2 646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2001\par 14:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 3 (Reuters) - The euro rose on Tuesday as gains of almost one percent against sterling dragged it broadly higher, even helping it reverse losses against the yen which had been triggered by comments from Japan's Prime Minister. \par \par \uc2  The yen was in the spotlight early on after Japan's Junichiro Koizumi said he had no intention of deliberately driving the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower, his first substantive comments on yen policy since his recent election. \par \par \uc2  But the euro soon became the biggest mover as profit-taking drove sterling back from recent one-month peaks against the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in thin trading before the U.S. holiday on Wednesday and a European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting on Thursday. Its gains came despite data showing economic sentiment in the euro zone had fallen for the sixth month in a row. \par \par \uc2  "The market did not like euro being below 60 pence and this has given the euro a lift across other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Neil Parker, economist at Royal Bank of Scotland Financial Markets. \par \par \uc2  "Markets are thin and there could also be some short-covering ahead of the ECB meeting. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said weak euro zone data has raised expectations the ECB may cut rates by a quarter-point this week and were eagerly awaiting a speech by ECB President Wim Duisenberg before the European parliament later in the day. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading at day's highs near $0.85 at 1200 GMT, having recovered from lows around $0.8455 set earlier after the European Commission said its economic sentiment index fell to 101.1 in June. It rose to day's highs around 105.50 yen . \par \par \uc2  WEAK DATA \par \par \uc2  The gloomy euro zone economic and business confidence data come only a day after reports signalled euro zone manufacturing activity contracting at a faster pace. \par \par \uc2  The fragile state of the euro zone economy was also highlighted by earlier data showing a deterioration in French consumer confidence. The French Insee consumer confidence index dropped to minus eight in June from a revised minus-six the previous month. \par \par \uc2  Traders said there was little appetite for new positions ahead of the U.S. holiday and the ECB meeting. \par \par \uc2  "Euro zone activity is deteriorating at a time when the U.S. economy is showing signs of stabilising," said Ian Gunner, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro. \par \par \uc2  "The euro has been hurt by the confusion that surrounds the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary stance and a lack of confidence in its ability to handle the situation." \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut interest rates only once this year in contrast to the Federal Reserve which has cut six times in an effort to stimulate growth. \par \par \uc2  KOIZUMI BOOSTS YEN \par \par \uc2  The euro's moves against sterling and the dollar saw it recoup ground against the yen, which had been strengthening early on in the European session. \par \par \uc2  The yen had earlier benefited from the comments made by Japan's Koizumi in an interview with the Financial Times which helped knock the dollar back more than a yen from Monday's 2-1/2 month highs. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the timing of the comments, so soon after Koizumi's weekend summit with U.S. President George W. Bush, seemed to put the final nail in the coffin of speculation of a joint U.S.-Japan agreement to promote a weaker yen to facilitate reform. \par \par \uc2  "The Koizumi statement is one of the first explicit comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from him we've had," said Jeremy Hawkins, chief economic adviser at the Bank of America. \par \par \uc2  Hawkins added that the comments had helped fuel wariness of possible Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falling too rapidly. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has shed some five yen against the dollar in the last month and is down more than eight percent since the start of the year. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010912dx7300fq9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
