\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar profits from gloom on euro zone economy. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sumeet Desai \par \uc2 404 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2001\par 14:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 20 (Reuters) - The dollar rose nearly a third of a percent against the euro on Wednesday as traders continued to take a pessimistic view about the euro zone's growth prospects in the light of recent weak economic data. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that while there had been little fresh fundamental news to push the euro down, it was being damaged by its failure to capitalise on gains last week and by more evidence this week of slowing European growth. \par \par \uc2  "All the European economic data seem to be pointing one way. People are now looking to see whether European officials are concerned about the fall in the euro," said Michael Metcalfe, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Agricole Indosuez. \par \par \uc2  "Unless they restore the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk, euro/dollar could slide further," he said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's gains against the euro pushed it higher by aorund a third of a percent versus the yen. \par \par \uc2  Prior to that, the yen had held steady in the face of a shrinking Japanese trade surplus and the government downgrading its assessment of the country's economic prospects as traders fretted over Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Masaru Hayami's warning on Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be needed if exchange rates moved too rapidly. \par \par \uc2  At 1140 GMT, the dollar was trading around 123.20 yen and $0.8513. Meanwhile, the euro was hardly changed from its New York close against the yen at 104.90. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the euro had also been receiving some support from rumours that European national central banks were protecting the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from falling below $0.8530. \par \par \uc2  "When the talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bids proved to be wrong as that level was taken out, the dollar went higher," said Neil Parket, market strategist at RBS Financial Markets. \par \par \uc2  A report showing Italian industrial orders falling an annual 7.9 percent in April had little market impact but underlined the weakness of the euro zone economy, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The head of Germany's DIW Insititute warning that Germany could fall into recession added to the general gloom. \par \par \uc2  Traders were waiting for Fed Chairman Alan Greenspan to appear before the Senate Banking Committee later on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Otherwise, focus will remain on Thursday's meeting in Dublin of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governing Council. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters last week gave a 70 percent likelihood that the ECB would keep rates steady. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6k0132e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
