\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen holds ground in face of worsening Japan prospects. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sumeet Desai \par \uc2 414 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2001\par 12:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 20 (Reuters) - The yen was steady on Wednesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  warning given a day ago by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief overshadowed a fall in Japan's trade surplus and a downgrade of the government's assessment of economic prospects. \par \par \uc2  Japan's trade surplus shrank by 86 percent in May from a year earlier while a draft of a government report obtained a day before publication said Japanese growth this financial year will be "significantly lower" than the initial 1.7 percent estimate. \par \par \uc2  But traders were wary of driving the yen down too far in the light of the warning issued on Tuesday by BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami, who said a weaker yen was not warranted and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be necessary if \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved too quickly. \par \par \uc2  "The yen has held up pretty well in the face of more bad news on Japan," said Nick Stamenkovic, strategist at Nomura International. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the euro was also little changed against the dollar, ignoring a 7.9 percent annual drop in Italian industrial orders in April. \par \par \uc2  At 1012 GMT, the dollar was trading at 123.07 yen, nearly a yen short of the one-month highs set on Tuesday, and at $0.8530 per euro. Euro/yen was holding around 105 yen. \par \par \uc2  EURO ON BACK FOOT \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the euro appeared to have failed to capitalise its gains made toward the end of last week after complaints by U.S. manufacturers about dollar strength spooked euro bears. \par \par \uc2  Weak euro zone industrial output numbers and a comment from German Economics Minister Werner Mueller that economic growth in the euro zone's largest economy could fall to zero in the second quarter on Tuesday did not help the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's cause. \par \par \uc2  "All the European economic data seem to be pointing one way. People are now looking to see whether European officials are concerned about the fall in the euro," said Michael Metcalfe, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Agricole Indosuez. \par \par \uc2  "Unless they restore the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk, euro/dollar could slide further," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers were also waiting for Fed Chairman Alan Greenspan appears before the Senate Banking Committee later on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Otherwise, focus will remain on Thursday's meeting of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governing Council on Thursday which is taking in place in Dublin this time. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters last week gave a 70 percent likelihood that the ECB would keep rates steady. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6k012xj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
