\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen claws back ground after BOJ warning. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 609 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2001\par 14:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 19 (Reuters) - The yen recovered from one-month lows against the dollar on Tuesday after Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Masaru Hayami said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be needed if exchange rates moved too rapidly. \par \par \uc2  Hayami also said Japan should not drive the yen lower due to the impact on neighbouring countries. \par \par \uc2  His comments had helped drive the yen up 0.75 percent from its lows against the dollar by the European midsession and Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also benefited against a broadly weak euro, rallying by more than 0.5 percent to the week's highs. \par \par \uc2  "The Hayami comments show Japan doesn't want to see the yen rapidly weaker. That's because of concern about the destabilising effect it would have on the economy," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  "But until we get a clear presentation of policy the market is going to be sceptical of Japan," he added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading around 123.05 yen at 1150 GMT according to Reuters data, around a fifth of a yen above the day's lows. The euro also was trading near its lows at around 105.30. \par \par \uc2  The euro, meanwhile, weakened to five-day lows against the dollar on continuing gloom about the euro zone economic outlook, and was trading near the bottom of a crucial support band of $0.8550/70. \par \par \uc2  ECONOMIC PAIN \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yen suffered in Tokyo trade as the market fretted over the pain the Japanese economy would have to go through to tackle structural reforms. \par \par \uc2  Rumours of a corporate failure at a Japanese retailer or construction company also helped the dollar in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Shares of Japan's fourth-largest supermarket operator Mycal Corp hit record lows on Tuesday on market concerns about its financial health. A company spokeswoman said the talk was groundless, aiding the yen's recovery in Europe, traders said. \par \par \uc2  STABLE PRICES \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials, meanwhile, continued to emphasise their inflation-busting credentials ahead of the ECB's policy-setting meeting in Dublin on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  ECB board member Klaus Liebscher said the ECB needed to remain very vigilant on inflation and that the current euro exchange rate did not match euro-zone fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke said the ECB must focus on maintaining price stability in an environment of "huge insecurity". \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters last week gave a 70 percent likelihood the ECB would leave rates on hold this week. \par \par \uc2  The euro zone is suffering from rising inflation and slowing growth, analysts said, leaving the ECB's hands tied. \par \par \uc2  Euro zone inflation hit an eight-year high in May, data released on Monday showed, while euro zone industrial production data released on Tuesday showed a fall of 0.5 percent in April and rise of 1.6 percent year-on-year, its slowest year-on-year rise since July 1999. \par \par \uc2  "These data are contributing to more euro weakness," said Armin Mekelburg, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HypoVereinsbank in Munich. \par \par \uc2  But the euro found support from lingering wariness about possible ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly after Sweden's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acted aggressively to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week. \par \par \uc2  "The Riksbank is a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and rising inflation and, rather than raising interest rates, it has been forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Teis Knuthsen, chief strategist at SEB Merchant Banking in Copenhagen. \par \par \uc2  "The same model works for the ECB." \par \par \uc2  The Riksbank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a second straight trading session on Monday, lifting the crown to three-week highs by buying the crown for both dollars and euros. \par \par \uc2  The crown weakened from those highs on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6j01fue\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
