\par\par \b \uc2  Japan fires warning shot as yen bears scent blood. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Christina Fincher \par \uc2 542 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2001\par 17:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 19 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest warning on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  betrays growing concern that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deteriorating economy could put the yen under further pressure, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  Firing a shot across the bows of yen bears, Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Masaru Hayami said on Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be needed if exchange rates moved too rapidly. He also warned that a weaker yen would be detrimental to the global economy. \par \par \uc2  The yen has fallen some five percent against the euro and the dollar already this month on growing signs that Japan's economy is faltering. \par \par \uc2  Although Japan is unlikely to be too concerned about the current level of the yen, given the export-boosting benefits of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation, the timing of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest salvo suggests it is aware that more drastic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves could lie ahead. \par \par \uc2  "There are a number of red lights flashing in Japan's economy and the bank doesn't want yen losses to get out of hand," said Neil MacKinnon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Merrill Lynch. \par \par \uc2  Among the warning signs is the weakness of Japanese bank stocks, now testing the record lows set in October 1998 when Japan was last in the throes of financial crisis. Japan's benchmark stock average is also flirting with a three-month low, having lost some five percent last week alone. \par \par \uc2  VOLATILE TIMES AHEAD? \par \par \uc2  It is not just the state of Japan's economy that has raised the risk of more volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves. Growing concern over the U.S. economy, falls in technology stocks, and jitters over Argentina's new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan mean the global economy is also looking precarious. \par \par \uc2  "Hayami can sense trouble brewing and is making an early bid to stem downside risks for the yen," said Claudio Piron, strategist at Standard Chartered. \par \par \uc2  Hayami's comments helped the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bounce back a full yen from one-month lows around 123.75 to the dollar and 106.30 to the euro on Tuesday. But analysts doubted whether the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone would be able to stem selling pressure on the yen. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials sought to talk the yen higher earlier this year but did not prevent the yen sliding to a 2-1/2 year low near 127 against the dollar in early April. \par \par \uc2  Japan has made many forays into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in recent years and, with over $360 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, its firepower is not to be sniffed at. But the political will for a yen-buying spree is questionable at a time when Japan needs all the help it can get to bolster its economy. \par \par \uc2  Data last week showed Japan's economy contracted in the first three months of this year and Japan's finance minister has predicted the current quarter will be even worse, effectively admitting the world's second largest economy was slipping into recession. \par \par \uc2  "Japan has no choice but to allow the yen to weaken," said Nick Parsons, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threat is part of a clean-hands policy because \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not want to be blamed by its trading partners for deliberately weakening its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6j0160x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
