\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Options - Yen vols firm after intraday rebound. \b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2001\par 19:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CHICAGO, June 19 (Reuters) - Implied volatility for one-month yen options firmed on Tuesday as the yen rebounded from a one-month low against the dollar amid hints of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen. \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Masaru Hayami said overnight the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if the yen decline becomes too rapid. His comments helped the dollar/yen retrace from its intraday high of 123.75. \par \par \uc2  Volatility for front-end yen was 10.2/10.5 percent, up from 10.0/10.3 percent on Monday. Some options traders reported several reverse knock-out options from 127.00 to 129.00. Reverse knock-out options are European-style options, meaning they can be exercised only on their day of expiration. They become in-the-money when the price of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reaches a certain level, but they become worthless if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues in the same direction beyond a specified level. \par \par \uc2  The options in dollar/yen suggest bullish leanings in the options market. Traders with the reverse knock-out options expect the dollar to rise against the yen but no further than the knock-out trigger level. \par \par \uc2  The 25-delta one-month risk reversal was 0.5/0.1, favoring yen puts and hinting at a perceived downside for the yen. Risk reversals measure the bias in the options market and reflect the value traders assign to puts and calls that are equally out-of-the-money. \par \par \uc2  Implied volatility for one-month euro options was quoted at 10.5/10.9 percent, down from 10.8/11.1 percent reported on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The 25-delta one-month risk reversal was quoted at 0.4/0.1, favoring euro calls. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6j0140k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
