\par\par \b \uc2  Euro seen hitting new life lows unless ECB acts. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sumeet Desai \par \uc2 775 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2001\par 14:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 5 (Reuters) - The euro is poised to fall to new life lows unless the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps in to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a possibility thrown into doubt by recent comments from euro zone officials. \par \par \uc2  Eurogroup chairman Didier Reynders said late on Monday the euro's current level is not a concern at the moment. The remarks helped push the euro to fresh six month lows around $0.8420 in Asia on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  But even if the ECB were to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and buy euros, analysts said it would have little lasting effect unless negative sentiment toward the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had begun to change and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was moving upwards. \par \par \uc2  In the absence of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said the way has now cleared for a test of last November's low of $0.8370 and then the all-time low of $0.8230 as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to be pressured by a cocktail of slowing growth, rising inflation, and a lack of faith in the ECB. \par \par \uc2  "We see the euro going down further. The ECB appears to be less concerned about a level for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  than the speed at which it goes," said Michael Dicks, chief European economist at Lehman Brothers. \par \par \uc2  Reynders's comments ended the respite the euro had won on Monday after Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke and Japan's top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda raised the spectre of co-ordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Group of Seven countries. \par \par \uc2  Otherwise, the sell-off really started last week on the back of ECB President Wim Duisenberg's apparent lack of concern at the euro's exchange rate. Duisenberg said then the euro's level was not a threat to the ECB's price stability mandate. \par \par \uc2  These comments, which followed ECB Council Member Klaus Leibscher's assertion that conditions are different from the last time the ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , were read as a green light to drive the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower. \par \par \uc2  "You've got to take them at face value and not try and second guess them. If they say they're not bothered about the euro, then they're probably not going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a chief trader at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the ECB is likely less concerned with the euro's weakness than it was last year because the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not so different from year-earlier levels and hence there is a correspondingly smaller impact on the inflation rate. \par \par \uc2  "We don't think there will be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at these levels. The comments from Duisenberg and Leibscher suggest they're not too worried yet. It's not that down on the year and so is not adding that much to the year-on-year inflation rate," said Adrian Schmidt, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at RBS Financial Markets. \par \par \uc2  ECB WON'T WANT TO GO AGAINST MARKET \par \par \uc2  Traders also pointed out the ECB is unlikely to be willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the tide of market opinion seems to be against it. \par \par \uc2  They said the ECB will want to catch the market when the euro is already rising, otherwise any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks ending in failure. \par \par \uc2  Still, ECB officials will continue to repeat that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains a tool at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's disposal in answer to questions about the exchange rate as anything else could send the euro into a freefall which would actually warrant the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "If it (the euro) started losing a cent a day, then obviously they couldn't have that," said Lehman's Dicks. \par \par \uc2  JAPAN SEEN AS BIGGEST THREAT \par \par \uc2  Traders have been most concerned about the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on euro/yen by both the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the ECB as the current view is that the Bush administration in the U.S. is not that keen on co-ordinated action. \par \par \uc2  Consequently, the euro's value against the yen has seen the biggest gyrations. It fell below 100 yen for the first time in five months, only to bounce two yen on Monday and then come down another yen on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that given the weakness of the Japanese economy, the authorities there are unlikely to want a stronger yen. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda's comments that the euro's latest fall was not appropriate highlighted this but contradicted the assertion of his boss Masajuro Shiokawa last week that recent \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves were normal and did not warrant \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Still, traders speculated that recent buying of euros for yen seen by the Japanese postal fund Kampo could be some form of "covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " on behalf of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument 