\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro rises, then buckles to fresh year lows vs. dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Javier David \par \uc2 640 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 2001\par 18:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      NEW YORK, June 1 (Reuters) - The euro slipped to its \par \par \uc2  weakest level against the dollar this year for the second \par \par \uc2  consecutive day on Friday, after encouraging U.S. employment \par \par \uc2  data tempered market concerns about the economy's prospects. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's woes began overnight, when it sold \par \par \uc2  off to below 100 yen for the first time in five months, helping \par \par \uc2  the yen extend rapid and broad gains after Japanese Finance \par \par \uc2  Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves did not \par \par \uc2  warrant \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But Europe's common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  capitulated to selling \par \par \uc2  pressure that had been building since early in the session \par \par \uc2  after the Labor Department reported that employers cut 19,000 \par \par \uc2  jobs in May, compared with a downwardly revised 182,000 drop in \par \par \uc2  April. The report also showed that the unemployment rate \par \par \uc2  declined to 4.4 percent from 4.5 percent, defying Wall Street \par \par \uc2  economists' expectations of a rise to 4.6 percent. \par \par \uc2      Analysts predicted further weakness is in store for the \par \par \uc2  swiftly sliding euro. \par \par \uc2      "The pressure on the euro is going to remain," said John \par \par \uc2  McCarthy, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at ING Barings \par \par \uc2  in New York. "But I don't think we'll see it substantially \par \par \uc2  lower as long as euro/yen stays above 100 yen." \par \par \uc2  Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to 84.30 cents in midday U.S. \par \par \uc2  trade , its lowest since Nov. 27, 2000. It recovered \par \par \uc2  slightly to drift near 84.50, marginally lower on the day. \par \par \uc2  Against Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro had fallen as low as \par \par \uc2  99.90 yen during London trade, its deepest trench since \par \par \uc2  December 2000. But by midday, it bought 100.60 yen \par \par \uc2  , off its Asia trading high above 101.10 yen and 0.20 \par \par \uc2  percent lower on the day. \par \par \uc2  The euro this week has derived minimal support from a fear \par \par \uc2  that European monetary officials could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its defense \par \par \uc2  by buying euros. \par \par \uc2  "People are afraid to be short, so once we pushed to lows \par \par \uc2  we saw a bit of a short squeeze," said Michael King, trader at \par \par \uc2  Commerzbank. "But any significnt rally should be sold into \par \par \uc2  this." \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar rose off fresh three-month lows hit \par \par \uc2  overnight, to trade near 119 yen in afternoon trade. It has \par \par \uc2  been largely weighed down by the euro's losses against the \par \par \uc2  Japanese unit. \par \par \uc2  MORE TALK FROM JAPAN DEEPENS EURO'S WOES \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa's comments came a day after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Council member Klaus Leibscher and ECB head Wim Duisenberg \par \par \uc2  appeared to rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the euro, sending \par \par \uc2  the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to six-month lows against the dollar on \par \par \uc2  Thursday. \par \par \uc2  But market participants have speculated that remarks out of \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Europe downplaying the prospects of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  could be a red herring to divert the market's attention, and \par \par \uc2  that the central banks could leap in to support the single \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when traders least expect. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that such action should not be ruled out \par \par \uc2  given the euro's heavy falls which has translated into \par \par \uc2  staggering yen gains, which could damage the already-fragile \par \par \uc2  economy. \par \par \uc2  "Shiokawa's comments have led to a feeling that \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely soon," said Arjun Mittal, economist at \par \par \uc2  American Express Bank in London. "But we would say that this \par \par \uc2  does not preclude the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the dollar displayed muted reaction to the \par \par \uc2  National Association of Purchasing Management's May \par \par \uc2  manufacturing survey, released early in the session. The \par \par \uc2  headline index checked in at 42.1 against 43.2 in April. \par \par \uc2  In other trading, the Canadian dollar edged off its highest \par \par \uc2  level in nearly a month against the dollar, buoyed by data on \par \par \uc2  Thursday showing Canada's gross domestic product rose to an \par \par \uc2  annualized 2.5 percent in the first quarter. It drifted near \par \par \uc2  1.5310 in afternoon dealings. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6102k2o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
