\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro drops below 100 yen, hurt by Japan comments. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Dhara Ranasinghe \par \uc2 596 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 2001\par 12:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 1 (Reuters) - The euro fell below 100 yen for the first time in five months on Friday, as the yen extended broad gains which began in Asia after Japan's Finance Minister said recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves did not warrant \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The comments by Masajuro Shiokawa also undermined the dollar against the yen, with the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest push higher against the euro triggering a move to new three-month lows on dollar/yen, which was left down 0.5 percent on the day. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa's comments came a day after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Council member Klaus Leibscher and ECB head Wim Duisenberg appeared to rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to up the prop the euro anytime soon, sending the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to six-month lows against the dollar on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The comments are partly a reason for the yen's strength as they suggest there is little concern about \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from either European or Japanese officials," said Mitul Kotecha, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Credit Agricole Indosuez in London. \par \par \uc2  The euro fell below 100 yen for the first time since December 19 according to Reuters data, before recovering to around 100.50 by 0939 GMT but still down more than a quarter percent on the day. \par \par \uc2  However, the euro was broadly steady against the dollar as the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept pace with its losses against the yen. The dollar fell as far as 118.32 yen , its weakest since March 6 and down almost one percent from Friday highs, with its latest losses coming before the key U.S. jobs report at 1230 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters expect, on average, May U.S. payrolls will show a decline of 17,000, against a 223,000 fall in April. The jobless rate is expected to rise to 4.6 percent from 4.5 percent the month before. \par \par \uc2  The euro showed little reaction earlier to Purchasing Managers' surveys from France, Italy and Germany, which showed manufacturing output falling in all three countries in May and French consumer confidence also fell in May. \par \par \uc2  The euro also showed little reaction to data showing the euro zone Purchasing Managers Index fell to its lowest since January 1999. \par \par \uc2  MARKETS STILL WARY \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that although comments by senior European and Japanese officials appeared to lower the chances of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such action should not be ruled out given the euro's heavy falls and concerns in Japan that a strong yen will hurt the already fragile economy. \par \par \uc2  "Shiokawa's comments have led to a feeling that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely soon," said Arjun Mittal, economist at American Express Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "But we would say that this does not preclude the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Traders added the ECB was also likely to get jittery if the euro fell further given its mandate for keeping inflation under control. \par \par \uc2  "The ECB's objective is price stability so the euro must be a concern despite recent comments suggesting that it isn't," said a London-based trader. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the yen's apparent strength could also be seen as an adjustment of excessive weakness since April, which had largely stemmed from assumptions that the Japanese government would guide the yen down. \par \par \uc2  The market was seen switching its focus to U.S. data due later in the day, with the National Association of Purchasing Management's May manufacturing index also due for release. \par \par \uc2  The headline index is forecast to rise to 43.5 from 43.2 in April. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6102ivx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
