\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro supported as  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  wariness grows. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sabrina Ghani \par \uc2 622 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2001\par 12:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 28 (Reuters) - The euro gained almost a quarter percent against the yen and was steady against the dollar on Monday as wariness of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action in its support discouraged another assault on the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  These concerns were stoked earlier by Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Haruhiko Kuroda who said that, taking into account economic fundamentals, there was a need for the euro to recover against the dollar and the yen. \par \par \uc2  With the euro holding a cent above last week's six-month lows against the dollar and three yen above five-month lows against the yen, the market wants to see if European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg echoes similar concerns in testimony before the European parliament's economic committee. \par \par \uc2  "There are expectations the ECB and the BOJ could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which could help the euro," said Philip Meyer, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Societe Generale in Paris."But the markets will be calm today with the U.S. and UK closed." \par \par \uc2  British markets were shut on Monday for the Spring Bank Holiday, and U.S. markets were due to be closed for the U.S. Memorial Day holiday. \par \par \uc2  At 0941 GMT, the euro was trading around $0.86, stuck in within a 1/3 cent trading range. It was holding at around 104 yen ahead of Duisenberg's speech later in the day. \par \par \uc2  The yen also fell against the dollar, trading around 121 yen per dollar, down about a quarter percent. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda also said he had not changed his mind that recent moves in dollar/yen were inappropriate. The dollar hit a three-month low around 118.80 yen last week having recoiled sharply from 124.00. \par \par \uc2  Since Friday, the euro has clawed back some of the three percent losses against the dollar and eight percent losses against yen it racked up last week, helped by comments from the ECB council member Ernst Welteke on Friday. \par \par \uc2  In a German newspaper Welteke was reported as saying that the euro's weakness has contributed to driving up inflation and that the exchange rate was an important factor for the ECB. \par \par \uc2  The euro's steep fall against the yen has also raised the prospect of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  either alone or in conjunction with the ECB to support the euro and restrain the yen and Kuroda's comments were a reminder the ECB was not alone, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Some traders suggested the central banks could be minded to take advantage of the lack of liquidity on a holiday to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  later on Monday, so getting more bang for their buck. \par \par \uc2  But others said any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely. \par \par \uc2  "There is talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but I think it is unlikely today and central banks are more likely to do it when the euro is going up," said a trader at a European bank. \par \par \uc2  "I don't expect Duisenberg to give any surprises away on euro/dollar thinking." \par \par \uc2  The euro meanwhile showed little reaction to data showing German import price inflation rose to a higher-than-expected 5.1 percent in April year-on-year from 4.2 percent in March, indicating that price pressures in Europe's largest economy are not abating. \par \par \uc2  The main cause for the euro's recent woes has been a run of surprisingly high inflation numbers in the euro zone coupled with disappointing economic growth data. \par \par \uc2  This triggered talk of stagflation, though many analysts consider this way overdone given that past episodes of stagflation have boasted inflation rates of 10 percent of more while the present rate was nearer three percent. \par \par \uc2  Inflationary pressures are seen limiting the scope for further policy easing to support economic growth. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx5s02ysx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
