\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro inches up on yen,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  eyed. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Isabel Reynolds \par \uc2 648 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2001\par 08:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 28 (Reuters) - The yen slipped a little against the euro in thin trade on Monday, but only fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prevented bears from launching another attack on the struggling single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Talk of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been supporting the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Friday, after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  council member Ernst Welteke's comments about the inflationary effects of euro weakness were published in a German newspaper. \par \par \uc2  The focus now turns to ECB President Wim Duisenberg, due to speak before the European parliament's economic committee later in the day, to see if he will echo these concerns. \par \par \uc2  On Monday morning, the market got a reminder that the ECB is not alone in its concern over the euro. \par \par \uc2  Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Haruhiko Kuroda said that, taking into account economic fundamentals, there was a need for the euro to recover against the dollar and the yen. \par \par \uc2  He added he had not changed his mind that recent moves in dollar/yen were inappropriate. The dollar hit a three-month low around 118.80 yen last week having recoiled sharply from 124.00. \par \par \uc2  In Tokyo, the yen drifted lower against the dollar, standing at around 121.05 in late afternoon trade, compared with 120.60 in New York on Friday. Public holidays in the United States and United Kingdom kept flows to a minimum. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had slipped to around $0.8585 by late afternoon, after bouncing to $0.8608 in New York from six-month lows around $0.8495. \par \par \uc2  It gained on the yen to stand at 103.86 yen having suffered a gut-wrenching slide to five-month lows near 101.00 last week. \par \par \uc2  That raised the prospect of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  either alone or in conjunction with the ECB to support the euro and restrain the yen. \par \par \uc2  Some traders suggested the central banks could be minded to take advantage of the lack of liquidity on a holiday to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  later on Monday, so getting more bang for their buck. \par \par \uc2  But others said any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely a long way off. \par \par \uc2  "The ECB is not like the Bank of Japan (BOJ)," said a trader at a Japanese bank. "It doesn't let people know when it plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so it will probably happen when everyone has forgotten about it." \par \par \uc2  LOSS OF FAITH \par \par \uc2  The immediate focus was on the testimony by ECB President Wim Duisenberg, but some traders were inclined to be cynical about the significance of his words. \par \par \uc2  "I can't see the euro going up just because the ECB President says something. Until \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  actually happens, it will be difficult to buy the euro," said the Japanese bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Their attitude is due in part to the fact that many Japanese investors were caught out by the euro's steep fall last week. \par \par \uc2  "A lot of people were caught under-hedged and the fear is that the euro will keep falling and cause some serious \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses," said a U.S. bank dealer, noting that Japanese investors were all too familiar with such behaviour. \par \par \uc2  "So a lot of these guys are praying for a bounce to sell into. That'll cap the upside and could make a slide self-fulfilling," he added. \par \par \uc2  Another cause of the euro's woes has been a run of surprisingly high inflation numbers in the euro zone coupled with disappointing economic growth data. \par \par \uc2  This triggered talk of stagflation, though many analysts consider this way overdone given that past episodes of stagflation have boasted inflation rates of 10 percent of more while the present rate was nearer three percent. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, in so much as this topped the ECB's self-imposed, and perhaps needlessly ambitious, inflation target of 2.0 percent it did limit the scope for further policy easing to support economic growth. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx5s02xwi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
