\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro rally against dollar proves short-lived. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2001\par 12:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 17 (Reuters) - The euro fully reversed 1/4 percent gains it made to one-week highs against the dollar earlier on Thursday, as talk subsided of European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and merger-inspired buying. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar retreated from recent highs against the yen after a Japanese press report got traders talking anew about the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem yen weakness. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the short-lived nature of the euro buying was likely to bring back into focus the positive impact of this week's half-point rate cut on U.S. assets, and therefore on the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "There were no fundamental reasons for the euro to be rising," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi in London. \par \par \uc2  "There was a big order that went through yesterday and the market cannot understand the reason behind it, so anything starts to appear possible." \par \par \uc2  The euro rose as far as $0.8880 and 109.30 yen, before retreating to $0.8820 and 108.80 by 0955 GMT. Talk a European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was selling dollars for Swiss francs also took the dollar briefly to a two-week low of 1.7266 francs. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading around 123.20 yen, a little above the day's lows and nearly one yen below May highs set on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  EURO RUMOURS \par \par \uc2  The euro extended gains made on Wednesday and in Asia on Thursday following a large order to buy euros for dollars by a German bank, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Speculation of the reasons for Thursday's short-lived gains varied from euro buying related to merger and acquisition activity, to buying by European central banks and to fund management purchases. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the temporary nature of such flows meant the euro's rise might stall in the face of the Federal Reserve's aggressive monetary easing to boost the U.S. economy, and were waiting to see how European operators would react to a sharp rise in U.S. stocks. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones Industrial average jumped 3.15 percent to an eight-month high in the wake of the Fed's fifth half-point rate cut on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the day's U.S. economic data would come under the spotlight as the market decides whether the Fed is likely to make another aggressive rate cut. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lowered rates five times this year, taking the federal funds rate to a seven-year low of 4.00 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The Philly Fed index is a fairly important figure and should attract attention because it is a reliable forward looking indicator," said Matthew Clements, economist at Prebon Marshall Yamane. \par \par \uc2  The Philadelphia Fed survey for May is due at 1400 GMT. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  WATCH \par \par \uc2  The yen was helped by an article in Japanese business daily Nihon Keizai saying that former Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa had discussed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a meeting of Asian finance ministers in April. \par \par \uc2  Analaysts said this had shifted the market focus back to whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the yen's recent weakness. \par \par \uc2  But \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Economics Minister Heizo Takenaka said late on Wednesday that the yen was not far from a convenient level. \par \par \uc2  In an interview with Reuters, Takenaka also said the yen would be influenced by the painful restructuring Japan will have to undergo, which traders took as tacit acceptance of a softer \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the yen was also helped on Thursday by a 1.58 percent rise in the benchmark Nikkei average, and data showed foreigners were net buyers of Japanese stocks last week for the eighth straight week. \par \par \uc2  But analysts added that, as with euro/dollar, moves in dollar/yen were likely to remain within recent broad ranges. \par \par \uc2  "It does not look like there is any enthusiasm for any of the G3 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Steven Englander, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Citibank. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx5h03lm2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
