\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED -  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro gains against broadly weak dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 660 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2001\par 10:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  In LONDON story headlined "Euro gains against broadly weak \par \par \uc2  dollar," please read in paragraph four...the dollar was trading \par \par \uc2  near the day's lows around 122.90 yen ... (Correcting the price \par \par \uc2  from 120.90). A corrected version of the story follows. \par \par \uc2  (Updates throughout, changes byline and dateline) \par \par \uc2  By Dhara Ranasinghe \par \par \uc2  LONDON, May 17 (Reuters) - The euro rose as much as a 1/4 \par \par \uc2  percent against the dollar and the yen on Thursday, with traders \par \par \uc2  citing a variety of reasons including possible mergers and \par \par \uc2  acquisitions activity and talk of European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bids. \par \par \uc2  The dollar, which hit one-week lows against the euro, was \par \par \uc2  also on the retreat against the yen after a Japanese press \par \par \uc2  report got traders talking anew about the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  to stem yen weakness. \par \par \uc2  "There are some rumours of European central banks and we \par \par \uc2  have also got talk of a big M&A deal," said a trader at a bank \par \par \uc2  in London. \par \par \uc2  The euro rose as far as $0.8880 and was pinned near the \par \par \uc2  day's peaks around 109.35 yen. Meanwhile, the dollar was trading \par \par \uc2  near the day's lows around 122.90 yen. \par \par \uc2  The yen was helped by an article in Japanese business daily \par \par \uc2  Nihon Keizai saying that former Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa \par \par \uc2  had discussed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a meeting of Asian \par \par \uc2  finance ministers in April had shifted the market focus back to \par \par \uc2  whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the yen's recent weakness. \par \par \uc2  "The article maintains the prospect of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \par \par \uc2  reminds the market and that it is still a possibility," said \par \par \uc2  Clememts from Prebon Marshall Yamane. \par \par \uc2  "Broad-based dollar weakness is also helping the yen." \par \par \uc2  EURO HOLDS GAINS \par \par \uc2  The euro extended gains it had made on Wednesday and in Asia \par \par \uc2  on Thursday following large orders to buy euros for dollar by a \par \par \uc2  German bank, traders said. \par \par \uc2  There was talk in Asia that the euro buying related to a \par \par \uc2  merger and acquisition activity in the telecoms sector and a \par \par \uc2  U.S. fund re-weighting its portfolio in favour of the euro zone, \par \par \uc2  but concrete evidence was lacking. In Europe, more reasons were \par \par \uc2  added to those. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the temporary nature of such flows meant \par \par \uc2  the euro's rise might be short-lived in the face of the Federal \par \par \uc2  Reserve's aggressive monetary easing to boost the U.S. economy \par \par \uc2  and were waiting to see how European operators would react to a \par \par \uc2  sharp rise in U.S. stocks. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones Industrial average jumped 3.15 percent to an \par \par \uc2  eight-month high in the wake of the Fed's fifth half-point rate \par \par \uc2  cut on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the day's U.S. economic data would fall under \par \par \uc2  the spotlight as the market decides whether the Fed is likely to \par \par \uc2  make another aggressive rate cut. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \par \par \uc2  lowered rates five times this year, taking the federal funds \par \par \uc2  rate to a seven year low. \par \par \uc2  "The Philly Fed index is a fairly important figure and \par \par \uc2  should attract attention because it is a reliable forward \par \par \uc2  looking indicator," said Matthew Clements, economist at Prebon \par \par \uc2  Marshall Yamane. \par \par \uc2  BUOYANT YEN \par \par \uc2  While the Miyazawa comments in the Nihon Keizai caught \par \par \uc2  traders eye, Japan's current finance minister, Masajuro Shiokawa \par \par \uc2  has shown no such inclination to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at least in public, \par \par \uc2  insisting that \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be left to the markets. \par \par \uc2  Economics Minister Heizo Takenaka said on Wednesday that the \par \par \uc2  yen was not far from a convenient level, echoing the relaxed \par \par \uc2  attitude of Shiokawa to recent yen movements. \par \par \uc2  In an interview with Reuters, Takenaka also said the yen \par \par \uc2  would be influenced by the painful restructuring Japan will have \par \par \uc2  to undergo, which traders took as tacit acceptance of a softer \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Exactly how soft was harder to say, though traders suspected \par \par \uc2  the authorities might become uncomfortable if the yen approached \par \par \uc2  130.00 to the dollar, in part because it would increase pressure \par \par \uc2  for competitive depreciations amongst other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx5h03dwn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
