\par\par \b \uc2  MOF says undecided on  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  disclosure. \b0\par\par\uc2 245 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2001\par 05:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, May 10 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) said on Thursday it has not yet decided whether to release information on its historic \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  following a report that it soon planned to make the data public. \par \par \uc2  Japan's Mainichi Shimbun newspaper reported on Thursday that the ministry is making final adjustments with the United States and Europe to disclose information about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  executed between April 1991 and March 2000. \par \par \uc2  The Mainichi said the ministry will complete the process by the end of the month and shortly after make it public, including the actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  dates and scale and type of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "At this stage, nothing had been decided," a senior MOF official said. "All I can say right now is that the report is based on speculation." \par \par \uc2  Japan, holding the world's largest external reserves at around $362 billion, began announcing quarterly base information on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from April 2000. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the ministry said it had not conducted any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the January-March period this year. \par \par \uc2  Last November, it said Japan had spent 143.5 billion yen during the July-September period in 2000, buying the beleaguered euro in joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with other Group of Seven nations in late September. \par \par \uc2  Before that, Japan had spent 1.385 trillion yen on dollar-buying, yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the April-June quarter in an attempt to prevent the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating sharply. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx5a00glr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
