\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF: No Foreign  \highlight22\uc2 Currency Intervention \highlight\uc2  In Jan-Mar \b0\par\par\uc2 127 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2001\par 03:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Wednesday the ministry did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets during the January to March period, as expected. \par \par \uc2  The ministry said it used zero yen in the first three months of the year for what it calls its "foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The last time the ministry reported using funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the July to September period of last year. The ministry sold Y143.5 billion of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for euros on Sept. 22 as part of a joint international effort to support the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By Audrey McAvoy, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par audrey.mcavoy@dowjones.com\par -0- 09/05/01 01-16G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx59024um\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
