\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr reclaims yen advantage, but faces resistance. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 1,018 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2001\par 02:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, April 9 (Reuters) - The dollar regained its advantage against the yen in Tokyo on Monday as Japan's stock market slipped and a statement on the yen after a weekend meeting of Southeast Asian finance officials failed to inspire buying. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar faced resistance at 125 yen, held in check by recent comments by Japanese finance ministry officials, after striking a high of 124.85 on bids led from Japanese importers in the morning, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At the end of a two-day meeting in Kuala Lumpur, finance ministers from the 10 members of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations "noted with concern the recent volatility of financial markets and the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly the depreciation of the Japanese yen." \par \par \uc2  Traders said the comment was pretty well expected. \par \par \uc2  "The communique was not surprising so the market is refraining from buying the yen further," said Hideaki Furumaya, head of interbank desk at Mizuho Trust & Banking Co Ltd. \par \par \uc2  "The ASEAN members have expressed their concern about the yen's depreciation but the content was in line with what the market had already factored-in last week," he said. \par \par \uc2  At 0310 GMT, the dollar stood at 124.72/82 yen against Friday's late U.S. level of 123.82/90. \par \par \uc2  But although yen fundamentals look bearish, the dollar is expected to face difficulties breaching last week's 2-1/2-year high of 126.84 yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They cite last week's yen-supportive comments by Japanese officials and fresh evidence of weakness in the U.S. economy on Friday when the U.S. Labour Department reported that non-farm payrolls fell 86,000 in March, the steepest monthly fall since November 1991 and well below expectations. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unemployment rate ticked up to 4.3 percent from February's 4.2 percent. \par \par \uc2  "As the Japanese economic fundamentals stay weak with the Nikkei slumping there is no reason to buy the yen actively," Furumaya said. "In this kind of situation, where we also can't buy the dollar, the dollar/yen rate should turn range bound." \par \par \uc2  ECB EYED \par \par \uc2  The euro firmed against the yen moving up in line with the dollar against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood at 112.64/79 yen against 111.86/2.02. It rested against the dollar at $0.9028/32 little changed from $0.9038/42 in late U.S. trade. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they were watching to see whether Japanese institutional investors will start investing in foreign securities, particularly the euro, in the near term. \par \par \uc2  Investors had been expected to buy strongly from the start of the fiscal year last week but this has been light so far, they said. \par \par \uc2  "We've seen some purchases from the start of the year, but the market has not yet seen major buying," a Japanese commercial bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "Most investors are probably waiting to see the decision from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to determine whether to invest more aggressively in the euro," he said, referring to the ECB's policy-setting meeting on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders are keeping an eye out for comments on the yen from MOF officials but most doubt that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at current levels unless the yen dips sharply toward 130 on the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda on Monday repeated his warning that Japan would take action if recent trends in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market continued, Jiji news agency said. \par \par \uc2  He was quoted as saying Japan will take appropriate action if the yen continues to move in a way that does not reflect fundamentals, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market showed little reaction. \par \par \uc2  ECB EYED \par \par \uc2  The euro firmed against the yen , moving up in line with the dollar against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood at 112.64/79 yen against 111.86/2.02. It rested against the dollar at $0.9028/32 , little changed from $0.9038/42 in late U.S. trade. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they were watching to see whether Japanese institutional investors will start investing in foreign securities, particularly the euro, in the near term. \par \par \uc2  Investors had been expected to buy strongly from the start of the fiscal year last week but this has been light so far, they said. \par \par \uc2  "We've seen some purchases from the start of the year, but the market has not yet seen major buying," a Japanese commercial bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "Most investors are probably waiting to see the decision from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to determine whether to invest more aggressively in the euro," he said, referring to the ECB's policy-setting meeting on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders are keeping an eye out for comments on the yen from MOF officials but most doubt that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at current levels unless the yen dips sharply toward 130 on the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda on Monday repeated his warning that Japan would take action if recent trends in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market continued, Jiji news agency said. \par \par \uc2  He was quoted as saying Japan will take appropriate action if the yen continues to move in a way that does not reflect fundamentals, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market showed little reaction. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0358 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2  Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2000 Cls \par \par \uc2  06 Apr. \par \par \uc2  ----------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab   0.9026   0.9038   -0.13    -4.95   0.9496\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab    124.82   123.74   +0.87    +9.06   114.45\par Euro/yen\tab \tab   112.66   111.82   +0.75    +3.63   108.71\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab  1.6939   1.6915   +0.14    +5.79   1.6012\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab    1.4384   1.4398   -0.10    -4.11   1.5000\par Can/dlr\tab \tab    1.5630   1.5642   -0.08    +4.80   1.4914\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab    0.4962   0.4982   -0.40   -11.30   0.5594\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab 1.5286   1.5293   -0.05    +0.43   1.5221\par Euro/stg\tab \tab   0.6276   0.6282   -0.10    -0.77   0.6325.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4902gaw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
