\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen racks up speedy gains on Japan warnings. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sabrina Ghani \par \uc2 885 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2001\par 09:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 5 (Reuters) - The yen rebounded one percent from recent 17-month lows against the euro and set one-week highs against the dollar on Thursday as top Japanese officials warned that further rapid yen falls would not be tolerated. \par \par \uc2  Delivering a veiled threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen, Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said the basic principle among the Group of Seven industrial nations was to resist any rapid moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  His deputy, Haruhiko Kuroda, was even blunter, saying Tokyo was prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless rapid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements abated, while Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Masaru Hayami warned against an overly rapid fall in the yen against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  While the euro fell against the yen, it outshone the dollar, hitting two-week highs to mark near four percent gains from Monday's 3-1/2 month lows, amid growing optimism that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would cut rates to stimulate growth. \par \par \uc2  "The Japanese officials have been out in force and they are serious about it," said Jesper Dannesboe, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein in London. \par \par \uc2  "That is why we are seeing a retracement in the yen. In dollar/ Y 123.50 yen is a key level and if we break that we could go to 122 yen." \par \par \uc2  Traders said the yen was also benefiting from a more than one percent rise in the Nikkei share average and expectations that an economic package to bolster its flagging economy and stocks would be unveiled on Friday. This contrasted with a more than two percent fall in the U.S. Nasdaq. \par \par \uc2  At 0730 GMT, the dollar was trading near one-week lows around 123.95 yen, down more than two yen from Monday's 2-1/2 year highs around 126.85 yen, according to Reuters data. \par \par \uc2  The euro fell to lows around 112.15 yen, down more than a yen from Wednesday's 17-month highs around 113.70. The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading just below earlier highs around around $0.9090 compared with Monday's lows around $0.8740. \par \par \uc2  Another factor supporting the euro against the dollar was Japanese investors' perception the safer way to play yen weakness was against the euro since the Japanese authorities were less likely to sell euros than dollars if they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders in Asia said. \par \par \uc2  The euro was already on the up against the dollar as a batch of weaker-than-expected euro zone data on Wednesday fanned expectations that the ECB could cut rates as early as next week. \par \par \uc2  "The market is awaiting some move by the ECB at the next meeting and a lot of the euro zone economic indicators do warrant some action," Neil MacKinnon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Merrill Lynch told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  "The sooner they cut rates the better (for the euro zone growth and the euro.)." \par \par \uc2  YEN GAINS SEEN LIMITED \par \par \uc2  While the yen was buoyant on Thursday analysts said its gains would be limited given Japan's economic and financial problems. \par \par \uc2  Most dealers agreed that the rash of comments marked a significant step-up in official rhetoric, but were unsure whether Japan merely wants to slow the yen's fall or stop it altogether. \par \par \uc2  "It's quite simple. The U.S. is complaining to Japan behind the scenes about guiding the yen down," said Takehiro Sato, economist at Morgan Stanley in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. can tolerate Japan's economy going downhill because of structural reforms and the weaker yen that will entail. But they will not tolerate a policy to push the yen down to support the economy. And that's what they are saying." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Kuroda had not made the ministry's task of managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  any easier by publishing a newspaper article that sowed confusion in the market. \par \par \uc2  A day after saying the yen's recent moves had been a little too rapid, Kuroda wrote in the Asian Wall Street Journal (AWSJ) that the depreciation was in fact largely in line with fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Asked by reporters to clarify his comments, Kuroda said, "It is true that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves over the past one to two weeks have been quite rapid. If \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves were to reflect fundamentals, the changes should be more gradual." \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Mainichi Shimbun daily reported on Thursday that members of the Association of South East Asian Nations would voice their concern about the weakening yen in a joint statement to be issued after their meeting in Malaysia this weekend. \par \par \uc2  South Korea has already made known its worries over the effect a rapidly weakening yen could have on its own economy by making its exports less competitive. \par \par \uc2  Though many Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  move to some extent in line with the yen, offsetting the export impact, this does not necessarily mean ASEAN nations would be happy with rapid changes in value, Gittler said. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, sterling hit one-week peaks against the dollar but fell to two-week troughs against the euro ahead of the Bank of England's interest rate decision later in the day. \par \par \uc2  In a Reuters poll, 18 economists out of 30 forecast a cut in repo rate from 5.75 percent but a dozen saw no change. Overall, they gave a 58 percent likelihood of a cut. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4502jqv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
