\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen rebounds from lows as dollar loses shine. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Christina Fincher \par \uc2 521 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 2001\par 10:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 3 (Reuters) - The yen rebounded one percent from recent 2-1/2 year lows against the dollar on Tuesday after Japan expressed concern about its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's swift decline. \par \par \uc2  Senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi said too rapid a fall in the yen was undesirable, echoing comments made a day earlier by Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa. \par \par \uc2  His comments sent dealers scrambling to lock in profits from the dollar's rise of about five percent against the yen in less than a week. The yen was also supported by anticipation of an emergency economic package to be announced by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ruling coalition, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "We are seeing verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and concern being expressed elsewhere in Asia about the yen's weakness," said Neil Mackinnon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Merrill Lynch. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean government also conveyed its concerns over the yen's rapid depreciation on Tuesday, saying it was talking to U.S. and Japanese authorities on the matter. \par \par \uc2  Having soared to a new 30-month high above 126.80 yen in New York, the dollar pulled back below 126 yen in early European trade. \par \par \uc2  The euro also recovered against the dollar to stand at $0.8860 , up from Monday's three-and-a-half month lows below $0.8750. \par \par \uc2  Dealers are looking to a raft of euro-zone industry and consumer data due out later on Tuesday to see if the weakness of Monday's PMI report is confirmed. \par \par \uc2  First off was French consumer confidence, which eased in March but remained in positive territory, registering two on the INSEE index after a revised four in February. \par \par \uc2  JAPAN PACKAGE \par \par \uc2  Anticipation of an emergency economic package to be announced by Japan's ruling coalition on Wednesday was also supporting the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Expectations about the measures pushed up Japanese share prices on Tuesday. The benchmark Nikkei average rose 1.44 percent, led by banking and real estate shares. \par \par \uc2  The proposals are to include the establishment of a fund to absorb the sale of Japanese banks' cross-held shares, as well as measures to improve liquidity in the real estate market. \par \par \uc2  Media reports say Japan's dominant Liberal Democratic Party will also announce on Wednesday the date for the party's election of its president, possibly on April 20. \par \par \uc2  Whoever takes over from gaffe-prone Prime Minister Yoshiro Mori as LDP president is almost guaranteed the premiership due to the ruling coalition's majority in parliament's Lower House. But the effect on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is uncertain as it is unclear who Mori's replacement will be. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Japanese exporters were offloading dollars as the greenback's bull run lost steam. Some saw a substantial correction in the offing. \par \par \uc2  "The market has a fear that the Japanese authorities may try to rein in the yen's fall. If they step up their efforts to talk up the yen, I think the dollar could fall as low as 123 yen," said Tetsuya Takahashi, assistant vice president at Bank of America in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx4302n3a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
