\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Japanese officials play football with yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 613 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 09:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 8 (Reuters) - The yen gyrated on Thursday, falling to 20-month lows against the dollar and then recovering, knocked around by conflicting comments from Japan's finance minister and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor. \par \par \uc2  The yen fell to its weakest level since July 1999 against the dollar after Japan's Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said the country's finances were near a state of collapse and fundamental fiscal reform was needed. \par \par \uc2  But the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered ground after Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami said a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in Japan's interests and the BOJ would keep sterilising liquidity stemming from \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The market is not particularly surprised at what Miyazawa is saying, but what is interesting is that he is prepared to say it so frankly," said Ryan Shea, international economist at Bank One in London. \par \par \uc2  "His comments are a backdoor method of weakening the yen." \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose as far as 120.40 yen, according to Reuters data, before retreating to 119.60/70 yen by 0820 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The euro approached 112 yen, a little below seven-week highs set on Wednesday, before easing to around 111.20. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said Miyazawa's comments were likely to have a stronger impact on the yen than those of Hayami. \par \par \uc2  "Miyazawa is in charge of whatever \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  does in terms of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the degrees of freedom Japanese policy-makers have are very small - a weaker yen remains the most plausible option." \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded a narrow range against the dollar around the $0.93 level. \par \par \uc2  German Finance Minister Hans Eichel said German economic growth had weakened slightly but was still robust, and forecast Europe would grow faster than the United States this year. \par \par \uc2  Preliminary fourth quarter growth data for the euro zone are due at 1100 GMT, and are forecast to show year-on-year growth of 3.1 percent. \par \par \uc2  POLITICS, ECONOMICS AFFECT YEN \par \par \uc2  The yen was earlier undermined on Thursday by Japanese machinery orders data, which showed a 11.8 percent drop in January from the previous month, far worse than the 6.1 percent fall analysts had been expecting. \par \par \uc2  The yen had already been on the defensive after a remark from Miyazawa on Wednesday that a weaker yen was fine as long as it happened naturally. \par \par \uc2  "It's clear they've sanctioned a lower yen as practically the only thing they can do for the economy in the short run," said a U.S. bank dealer in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "Even easing policy further wouldn't have much effect if it's not accompanied by real structural reform, and Japan's politics make that unlikely just now," the dealer added. \par \par \uc2  Japanese politics are practically paralysed as the ruling party prepares to oust the unpopular Yoshiro Mori and replace him as prime minister with someone more electorally viable. \par \par \uc2  Given that outlook, analysts and dealers were almost unanimous in their expectations for a lower yen. \par \par \uc2  A$ HITS RECORD LOW \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar, meanwhile, fell to record lows against the U.S. dollar, crushed by weak data and a quarter point interest rate cut on Wednesday which removed Australia's former interest rate advantage over the United States. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar fell to a low of US$0.5067 in early European trade, surpassing the previous record low set in late November. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was steady ahead of a rate announcement after the Bank of England's two-day policy-setting meeting and following the 2001 budget on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  A majority of economists expect no change in the repo rate, currently at 5.75 percent following a quarter point cut last month. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3804pjq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
