\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ Hayami: Repeats Economy Not In Deflationary Spiral \b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 06:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Masaru Hayami said Thursday that using \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen as an economic policy step would have its problems and thus be difficult. \par \par \uc2  "Using \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has its problems and would be difficult," Hayami said, adding that he had meant to imply the same message during a speech Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Speaking in Parliament, Hayami said Thursday he was "displeased" with local media reports interpreting a reference he made to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as being a conceivable policy option. \par \par \uc2  Hayami's comments in Upper House budget committee were the second time Thursday that he criticized news reports which implied he was advocating artificially weakening the yen through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In a speech given Wednesday, Hayami said that "From the standpoint of drastic measures that could be tried, guiding the yen sharply lower through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one thing that is conceivable," but he immediately expressed doubts over using such as policy due to its adverse impact on Asia and import prices. \par \par \uc2  Market players - looking at the first part of the comments which were put out on wires by a Japanese news agency - initially interpreted the comments to mean that the BOJ was advocating the use of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to achieve a weak yen. \par \par \uc2  "I made the comment to show that there are some opinions like that around," and not to show the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's intention of actually seeking such a step, Hayami said. \par \par \uc2  Turning to the issue of directly underwriting Japanese government bonds as a means to reflate the economy, Hayami said that the BOJ "has absolutely no intention" of considering this. \par \par \uc2  Direct underwriting of JGBs - a radical move which is effectively synonymous with printing money - is banned under Japan's current Fiscal Law after it caused hyper inflation in the past. \par \par \uc2  Hayami refered to both the past bout of hyper inflation and the fact that the move is banned by law, emphasizing that there is no way that the BOJ will conduct the step. \par \par \uc2  Direct underwriting is different from recent calls on the BOJ to increase its outright purchases of JGBs as a quantitative easing step. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par miyako.takebe@dowjones.com\par -0- 08/03/01 07-14G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx38012g3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
