\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets-Lifted by tech gains,  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  wilt. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Anchalee Worrachate \par \uc2 813 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 10:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, March 7 (Reuters) - Asian stocks raked in \par \par \uc2  moderate gains on Wednesday after a rebound in the tech-laden \par \par \uc2  Nasdaq, but investors promptly took profits in most markets. \par \par \uc2      Japan's benchmark Nikkei 225, for example, ended a mere \par \par \uc2  0.28 percent higher at 12,723.89 after rising by 1.07 percent \par \par \uc2  earlier. \par \par \uc2      Traders said Tokyo investors were quick to take profits due \par \par \uc2  to lingering doubts over Japan's fragile economy and political \par \par \uc2  uncertainty. \par \par \uc2      South Korea's KOSPI also ended marginally higher, helped by \par \par \uc2  heavy foreign buying of Samsung Electronics which outweighed \par \par \uc2  losses in other key blue chip shares. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said the recent buying of tech stocks was purely \par \par \uc2  technical as downside risk was still intact in the near term. \par \par \uc2      "There is no reason for rushing in. I still see downside \par \par \uc2  risk for tech stocks in the near term due to utter lack of \par \par \uc2  visibility in the industry. Nobody is giving suppliers any \par \par \uc2  guidance," said David Toh, technology analyst at ING Barings. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  HELD HOSTAGE TO YEN \par \par \uc2  Confusion over an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remark made by Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Governor Hayami Masaru sparked yen selling, pulling down with \par \par \uc2  it other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Masaru had earlier mentioned in a speech that one drastic \par \par \uc2  policy option put to the bank had been to substantially weaken \par \par \uc2  the yen through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The market took the comment as a signal for a softer yen \par \par \uc2  and rushed to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \par \par \uc2  deny that Hayami ever implied the bank would actually use \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The Thai baht dipped below 43.50 while the Korean won whose \par \par \uc2  direction is mostly dictated by the yen, also ended lower. \par \par \uc2      THAILAND AWAITS AMC DETAILS \par \par \uc2      Thai stocks perked up on Thursday on the back of buying of \par \par \uc2  banks and finance shares amid hopes the government would come \par \par \uc2  up with positive details on its planned national asset \par \par \uc2  management company (AMC). \par \par \uc2  A government committee will meet bankers to decide on \par \par \uc2  discounts for non-performing loans after the market closes on \par \par \uc2  Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The committee has said it intends to buy around 330 billion \par \par \uc2  of bad loans owned by state banks, 500 billion baht worth of \par \par \uc2  NPLs from an existing asset management firm and around 120 \par \par \uc2  billion from private banks. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said if the committee set the discount rate too \par \par \uc2  high, banks would be discouraged to sell their bad assets to \par \par \uc2  the company because they might be forced to immediately book \par \par \uc2  substantial losses. \par \par \uc2  But given the politically-sensitive nature of the plan, the \par \par \uc2  government might not be willing to buy these assets at high \par \par \uc2  prices either, they said. \par \par \uc2  Some are more concerned about the transparency and \par \par \uc2  effectiveness of the whole centralised debt restructuring \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There is fear that these assets will be locked up and \par \par \uc2  forgotten about. There is also upsetting fear there will be all \par \par \uc2  sorts of sweetheart deals for friends of bureaucrats and \par \par \uc2  politicians," said Richard Henderson, research director at Kim \par \par \uc2  Eng Securities. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0827 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     119.29\tab  118.45\tab    -0.70\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7550\tab  1.7546\tab    -0.02\par  Taiwan dlr    32.370\tab  32.362\tab    -0.02\par  Korean won   1272.50\tab 1264.80\tab    -0.61\par  Baht\tab      43.51\tab   43.43\tab    -0.18\par  Peso\tab      47.85\tab   47.50\tab    -0.73\par  Rupiah\tab  9870.00\tab 9875.00\tab    +0.05\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.29\tab  114.45\tab    -4.06\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7550\tab  1.7365\tab    -1.05\par  Taiwan dlr    32.370\tab  32.900\tab    +1.64\par  Korean won   1272.50\tab 1277.00\tab    +0.35\par  Baht\tab      43.51\tab   43.70\tab    +0.44\par  Peso\tab      47.85\tab   50.75\tab    +6.06\par  Rupiah\tab  9870.00\tab 9470.00\tab    -4.05\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ASIAN STOCK MARKETS  0827 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Market\tab  Current\tab Prev Close     Pct Move\par  Tokyo\tab 