\par\par \b \uc2  Hayami - Yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  an option but need caution. \b0\par\par\uc2 186 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 06:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 7 (Reuters) - Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Masaru Hayami said on Wednesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to drive down the yen was among policy options presented to the bank, but he urged caution. \par \par \uc2  After listing a return to zero rates and quantitative monetary easing as possible bold steps suggested to the BOJ, Hayami added: "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets and driving down the yen is another policy idea. \par \par \uc2  "Under the current legal framework, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is up to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But that aside, it is uncertain how effective such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be in determining exchange rates," he said in a speech to business leaders and journalists. \par \par \uc2  "We would need to carefully consider the negative impact, such as higher import prices and the negative impact on Asian economies," he said. \par \par \uc2  Politicians in the Liberal Democratic Party, the dominant member in the three-way ruling coalition, have repeatedly called for a return to zero interest rates to help revive the economy. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ tried zero rates for 18 months but dumped the policy last August. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3704noy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
