\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen rallies to week's highs, euro biggest loser. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 946 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2001\par 14:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 14 (Reuters) - The yen rose to its highest this week against the dollar and the euro on Wednesday after Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor questioned the value of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a tool to weaken \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Attention switched from the broadly sagging euro to the yen after Bank of Japan governor Masaru Hayami said he was cautious about artificially weakening the yen. He also said it would be inappropriate to return to the BOJ's zero interest-rate policy. \par \par \uc2  "Hayami's comments about the yen have given the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a lift," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi in London. \par \par \uc2  By 1240 GMT the dollar was trading around the week's lows of 116.23 yen , according to Reuters data, while the euro bore the brunt of yen's strength, falling to the week's lows against below 107 yen . \par \par \uc2  Repatriation of funds into Japan as the fiscal year-end approaches was also keeping the yen afloat, analysts and traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The yen moves this morning have been flow-related - we have seen liquidation of European bond markets by Japanese accounts," said Hans-Guenter Redeker, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas in London. \par \par \uc2  The yen found additional support earlier on Wednesday from speculation that Japan's unpopular Prime Minister Yoshiro Mori may be forced out of office. \par \par \uc2  Yen buying was sparked by a report that an unidentified senior executive from the New Komeito Party, the number two party in Japan's ruling coalition, said Mori should resign. \par \par \uc2  Mori has been under sustained criticism for continuing to play golf after hearing that a U.S. submarine had crashed into and sunk a Japanese ship carrying students off Hawaii last week. \par \par \uc2  EURO TRAILS \par \par \uc2  The euro, meanwhile, softened as recent German data and remarks made a day ago by Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan fanned speculation the euro zone economy may not outperform the U.S. one as much as previously thought. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suffering in the wake of Tuesday's weaker-than-expected German retail sales data and stronger-than-expected U.S. retail sales, as well as Greenspan's cautiously optimistic assessment of the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  The figures and the scope for a relatively quick recovery in the slowing U.S. growth caught many traders who had taken a bullish view on the euro off guard, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The market seems to remain long of euros both against the dollar and against the yen. With the kind of data that we have been seeing, those positions are being exposed and that has led to a retracement," said Shahab Jalinoos, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg in London. The euro was trading around the day's lows of $0.9172 , down a quarter cent from Tuesday's New York close. \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief economist Otmar Issing said in an interview published on Wednesday that the ECB's monetary policy focused on price stability posed no threat to global and euro zone growth. \par \par \uc2  While traders said retail sales figures could often be quite volatile, particularly toward the end or the start of a year, they said Greenspan's comments supported a growing view in the market that the U.S. slowdown could be relatively shortlived. \par \par \uc2  Greenspan said on Tuesday there were downside risks to the U.S. economy but that the excessive weakness seen late last year had not followed through into January. \par \par \uc2  He also expressed confidence that the economy would pick up in the second half of the year once inventory correction had run its course and looked for gross domestic product growth of 2.0-2.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Greenspan's testimony placed further doubts about the euro's ability to reclaim parity, a feat which appeared almost a done deal a few weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  Concern about the health of the U.S. economy and its impact on U.S. asset markets helped the euro to recover by nearly 17 percent against the dollar by mid-January, from record lows of $0.8225 set at the end of October. \par \par \uc2  But the euro has since depreciated by 4.5 percent, and is in danger of further losses, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The $0.9150 level is key - if we break that we could go to $0.90 within a week," said a trader from a German bank in Frankfurt. \par \par \uc2  STERLING SPRIGHTLY \par \par \uc2  Sterling rose after a larger than expected 25,500 fall in claimant count unemployment in January and a stronger than expected 4.4 percent rise in average earnings in the three months to December was seen taking some off the pressure off the Bank of England to make further cuts in interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The BOE's policy-setting committee cut interest rates by 25 basis points earlier this month, to 5.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  Sterling extended its gains, hitting two-week highs against the euro around 63.00 pence and one-week highs against the dollar near $1.46 , after the BOE said in its quarterly inflation report that inflationary pressures were more benign, due to the effect of lower energy prices and slower economic growth. \par \par \uc2  The Swedish crown, meanwhile, fell to its lowest in more than two years towards 9.05 to the euro , hit by weakness in telecom equipment heavyweight Ericsson and other Swedish shares. \par \par \uc2  The crown's latest retreat also came after speculation of higher Swedish interest rates was dented by comments from Riksbank Governor Urban Backstrom, who said in a business magazine published on Wednesday that the U.S. economic slowdown meant there was less pressure for higher Swedish rates. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx2e06jle\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
