\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-ECB- \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves fall after Nov 9  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 447 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 2000\par 16:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  FRANKFURT, Nov 21 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and euro area central banks fell last week by a net 1.2 billion euros ($1.02 billion), partly due to its November 9 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ECB said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  This brought the cumulative fall in reserves for the past two weeks, which also included \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on November 3 and 6, to 5.8 billion euros. \par \par \uc2  The ECB said in its weekly financial statement the decline in reserves last week also reflected a swap transaction with the Bank of Japan and routine customer and portfolio transactions carried out by the euro area national central banks. \par \par \uc2  It gave no further indication of the volume of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and analysts said it was hard to calculate the exact amount of euros the ECB bought in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  But the numbers released by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the week to November 17 were in line with estimates that the volumes of this month's purchases were relatively small. \par \par \uc2  "It's difficult to offer an estimate based on such a marginal change as there are also other transactions that blur the picture," said Stefan Schneider, analyst at Deutsche Bank Research in Frankfurt. In the previous week \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves held by the ECB and euro area national central banks fell 4.6 billion euros and the ECB cited its euro buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on November 3 and 6 among the reasons for the drop. \par \par \uc2  Its last foray into \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets settled last week and was not covered by the previous statement. \par \par \uc2  Market players have estimated that the ECB had bought a total of around 3.5 billion euros in its solo \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this month with the last round of euro buying totalling around or below one billion euros. \par \par \uc2  Similarly to the previous week, the statement mentioned swap transactions with the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a sign that the ECB was buying euros against the yen as well as the dollar, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The ECB used a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap with the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  also in September when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time to prop up the euro, acting in concert with other Group of Seven industrial nations. \par \par \uc2  The swaps allow central banks to effectively borrow \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  they want to use for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against other assets, so they are not constrained by the composition of their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  The net position of the European system of central banks in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves totalled 270.7 billion euros at the end of the reporting week. Gold reserves were steady at 124.947 billion euros, the ECB said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwbl01h6t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
