\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro bounces amid  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  jitters. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shinichi Kishima \par \uc2 614 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2000\par 10:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 17 (Reuters) - The euro was firmer on Friday, bouncing from two-week lows against the dollar it had hit a day earlier amid persistent jitters of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro briefly spiked up by half a cent late in Asian trading as some large buying orders triggered mini-panic buying, with traders' nerves jangled by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's three rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  The ECB declined to comment on whether it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday - in its previous euro-buying sprees, it announced what it had done immediately after the action. But traders said speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could step in any time was keeping the market jumpy. \par \par \uc2  "There's still some concern about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and you hear about it almost every day," said Claudio Piron, treasury economist at Standard Chartered Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  While the euro remained vulnerable, the ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this month, which followed a joint Group of Seven effort in September, was starting to instill caution about aggressively selling the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Piron said. \par \par \uc2  "It's not going to turn it around, but if they successfully protect the downside of $0.85, it's going down in the history books, a bit like the Bank of Japan at 100 on dollar/yen." \par \par \uc2  ECB vice president Christian Noyer said on Friday policymakers must signal concerns about the euro extremely clearly, although the euro barely moved on his comments. \par \par \uc2  At 0815 GMT, the euro was at $0.8557/63 EUR=), according to Reuters data, up half a cent from two-week lows around $0.8510 hit late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The euro also drew some support from late Thursday news that MSCI, an asset allocation benchmark, had raised the capitalisation of its European equity index. \par \par \uc2  Morgan Stanley Capital International said it increased its Europe Index market capitalisation by 1.4 percent or $85 billion. These indices are closely tracked by many fund managers, so the rise in capitalisation could lead to foreign fund flows into some European equities. \par \par \uc2  In the United States, where the outcome of last week's presidential election hinged on legal wranglings in Florida, the state's supreme court ruled to allow hand counting of ballots. \par \par \uc2  That tended to favour Democrat Al Gore, who in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was considered to be more in favour of joining coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro than Republican George W. Bush. \par \par \uc2  Still, traders warned that the minutes of the U.S. Federal Reserve's October 3 policy meeting released on Thursday showed that its participation in the G7's September \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not a signal of increased willingness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  YEN AWAITS \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2  POLTICAL SHOWDOWN \par \par \uc2  The yen clawed back some of its recent losses against the dollar but traders said it could be prone to further volatility ahead of a political showdown on Monday, as rebels within Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party vowed to support a no-confidence motion in Prime Minister Yoshiro Mori's government. \par \par \uc2  If all the members of the rebel factions were to vote with the opposition, it would be enough to carry the motion and Mori will have to resign or call a national election. \par \par \uc2  "It could be we'll have a new prime minister next week and he might even be a reformer," said a European bank dealer in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "If so, that could be a plus for the yen and the economy, but until we know for sure, it's hardly a reason to buy yen." \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen JPY=) was trading at 108.65, about a half yen off Thursday's two-week highs. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwbh01g6s\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50